  :en-route "FOUR defects, three mine and one real, each caught by a wasm32 golden run or its isolation: (1) my replace-first multi-byte expectation wrote a replace-ALL answer (X本語xX) for a replace-FIRST operation (X本語x日); (2) my segment expectation ignored the 3-byte separator (segment 1 of x日本x by 日 is 本x, not x); (3) my pad-center golden ignored the never-split-a-fill overshoot (hi w3 fill ab is hiab, not hi); and the REAL one -- seg-after returned the text AFTER n separators without cutting at the next, answering segment 1 of a,b,c with b,c. Fixed by cut-at-sep at the base case."
